WEBVTT

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.740
<b>Let's head
 back home
 for the day!</b>

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.740
<b>That one step
 might be your 
chance to grab
 happiness.</b>

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.740
<b>Three years of
 standing on a 
cold stone makes
 you strong... 
Nah, maybe not.</b>

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.490
<b>That one step
 might be your chance
 to grab happiness.</b>

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.150
Excuse me...

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.900
Yes?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.490
P-Please read this.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.590
I fell in love with you at first sight.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.760
<i>Furukanata. Furukanata.</i>

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.210
<i>The doors on the left side will open.</i>

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.640
She bolted?!

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:15.300
No way!

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.050
Hime!

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.110
Wait!

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:27.200
<b>Local Train</b>

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:27.200
<b>Satose</b>

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.860
<i>The 8:00 AM local train bound for Satose</i>

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.170
<i>will be closing its doors momentarily.</i>

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:39.220
<b>Furukanata Station</b>

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.670
Why'd you run away?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.720
Uh...

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.920
Come on.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.160
Uh...

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.490
Seriously, why'd you run away 
without saying anything?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.350
Uh...

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.570
Come on! Why can't you tell me?!

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.410
Oh, good morning.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:04.140
Hey! Why didn't you take his letter?

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.700
Well, I mean...

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.920
I couldn't accept it.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.940
Tell me why!

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.080
I can't say it...

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.600
Come on, answer me.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.670
Uh...

00:03:21.850 --> 00:03:23.530
I'm too embarrassed.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.900
So...

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.860
Why'd you run away?

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.140
You're at home now,
 so no one else is listening.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.540
Can't you tell us now?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.780
That's right.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.770
He didn't seem like such a weird guy.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.540
Did his bald head bug you?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.470
No, he wasn't bald. He had a buzzcut.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:53.830
He seemed like a guy who's 
into sports, though.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.430
Really? I bet he smells sweaty, then!

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.180
He seemed pretty pleasant to me.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.860
You think so?

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:04.300
I didn't see any reason
 to run away, in any case.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.810
You're right, but...

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.930
Then why?

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.680
Well, I'm... scared.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.320
Of boys?

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:23.320
Wait, were you always like that?

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.180
You talk to Komori and Nekomi, though.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:30.700
Talking to them normally 
isn't a problem, but...

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.290
Well...

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:35.780
What?

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.850
I mean...

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:42.850
Wait, is it going out with 
a guy that scares you?

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.110
So... what is it you're afraid of?

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.670
I know!

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:52.970
Sexual stuff, right?

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.780
What, <i>that</i>?

00:04:57.370 --> 00:04:59.140
Wait, really?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.240
No, that's not it.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.650
Hime's not that type.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.360
So... it's what comes after that?

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.420
Is it getting pregnant?

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:16.020
They say being a hybrid of differently-shaped 
species makes childbirth tough for centaurs.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.160
We had a lesson about that once...

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:25.170
<b>All citizens qualifying as biologically intermediate 
are eligible to receive various forms of support to ensure that they are able to live a life without hindrances, and are not put at a disadvantage mentally or physically.</b>

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:25.170
<b>This guarantee is offered under 
the Second Article of the Constitution 
and applies to all citizens. However, 
concealing or falsifying one's criminal record, as well as failing to provide
 one's criminal record in compliance 
with the Third Article, are grounds for criminal charges.</b>

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.330
Well, that's why the government offers 
a guarantee to folks like that.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.190
What are you, a government bulletin?

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.110
Is that why?

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.410
What? It's not?

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:32.120
Then what are you afraid of?

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.650
Well...

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.300
When I was in kindergarten...

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.410
Does yours look like that, too?

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.520
No! That's a cow!

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.920
Will your boobs get huge, too?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.740
Um...

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:13.500
So... are you saying you're worried 
that yours is gross, too?

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.400
Well, he was right about your boobs.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.160
You idiot!

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.680
Have you ever looked at yourself?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.030
I'm afraid to.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.570
That doesn't give us much to go on...

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.860
Guys don't even worry about 
that kind of thing, anyway.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.870
<b>Health
 Education</b>

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.030
Especially when you're not even dating yet.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.390
But...

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.660
With a complex like this, 
I can't date anyone.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:49.130
Maybe not, but...

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.930
<b>Health
 Education</b>

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.930
Have you ever seen anyone else's, then?

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.300
Even at the pool or a public bath?

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:59.300
I don't want anyone to see mine, either,

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.000
so since I can't hide it...

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.060
I see...

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:06.370
Everyone else covers themselves 
when they change, you know?

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:07.520
Good point.

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:13.070
Of course, I asked that, 
but I've never seen anyone else's, either.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.230
Yeah, same.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:21.040
Still, this is a problem that won't go away 
unless you compare your own to someone else's.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.700
And that's what I'm afraid of!

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:25.320
Okay, I got it.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.260
I'll show you.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:33.540
Um... Show me what?

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.210
I'll show you mine.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.050
Me and Kyoko.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.380
Me, too?!

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.760
I don't want to!

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.050
Why?

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:42.490
Why?!

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:43.730
We're her friends, right?

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.710
That has nothing to do with it!

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:49.360
Okay, Hime, you can look at mine,

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.450
and we'll check yours for you.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.810
Then you can rest easy, right?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.980
Your breath is tickling me...

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.390
It's prettier than a cow's.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.960
Well, I'd hope so.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.320
It's unused.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:19.910
Hey!

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.030
Now...

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.250
You're next, Kyoko.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.450
F-Forget it!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.030
I don't think so!

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.380
Oh, it's hairier than I expected.

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.000
Stop looking!

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.750
Sorry... But now we're even.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.360
And now...

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:57.280
It's finally Hime's turn.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:03.370
Now, then!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.720
Sorry... How do you get this off?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.450
Oh, you've come back to life.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.800
It's pretty!

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.860
Sort of... youthful.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.950
Okay, isn't that long enough?

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.240
Hime, you can't see it yourself, right?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.980
So I'll take a picture.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.420
Say cheese—

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:36.870
Don't! I'll take your word for it!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.360
Hey!

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.410
You're totally okay.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:51.020
Feel better now?

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:54.650
Yeah.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:56.020
Huh?

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.020
Come on, Kyoko...

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.930
I'm sorry, okay?

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.980
But Hime feels better now,

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:07.130
so what's the problem?
 It didn't hurt anything.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.530
Come on, don't make that face!

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.140
<b>Furukanata Station</b>

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:51.830
Um...

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:57.720
<i>Furukanata. Furukanata.</i>

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:02.810
<i>The doors are now opening.</i>

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.810
I'm sorry!

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.300
Huh?!

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.330
Again?!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:08.590
Hime!

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:09.750
Wait!

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.600
<i>The doors are now closing.</i>

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.430
Why'd you turn him down?

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:23.710
And why'd you run away again?

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:25.360
Because...

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:32.840
His letter said stuff like, 
"Your breasts are so big and beautiful."

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.980
So it comes down to that, huh?

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:40.010
That's all boys think about.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:46.930
<b>Why Are We So Bewildered When 
We Receive a Love Letter?</b>

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:53.330
So the product here is...

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.110
And that one is...

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.440
I just don't get it!

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:03.450
Come on, Nozomi!

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.280
It hasn't even been half an hour!

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.210
Hey! Don't start reading manga!

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:12.250
Come on, Nozomi!

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.160
Listen...

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:25.290
Do you understand why we're having 
a study party on a Sunday?

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.310
<b>The following students will take 
supplementary lessons and a make-up test</b>

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:30.800
You're in trouble if you get another 
failing score on your next test.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.720
<b>299
 Gokuraku 
Nozomi</b>

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.630
Yeah, but still...

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:35.930
That tickles!

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:39.440
I can't memorize all these formulas!

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.440
<b>I don't get why 
it works out like this!</b>

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.920
Just thinking about it 
like that is a problem.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:45.560
This is still math, you know.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:49.690
It's not a bunch of puzzles. 
Memorizing formulas is all you can do.

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:53.790
There's a right way to think about it,
 so you need to understand that.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:58.040
That way, even if you forget the formula,
 you can find the answer.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.730
Look, my whole problem is 
that I <i>can't</i> do that!

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:06.970
I'm trying to help because 
you're in dire straits here.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.320
Hime, put her in a pinion 
hold, so she can't run!

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:12.430
R-Right!

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.490
Is this how you do a pinion hold?

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:16.390
No, it's not!

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:17.550
It doesn't matter!

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:19.970
Are you ready?!

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:23.030
Sure...

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:26.830
I'm about to drill math, 
English, science, physics,

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:28.810
and classic literature into your bones!

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.840
Nozomi-chan, open up.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:44.420
Like it?

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.130
It's sweet...

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:48.040
Keep that sugar level up.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:51.500
The brain uses more energy than 
any other organ, after all.

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.520
<b>Study Party</b>

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:56.350
You'll never be ready for the test 
in time at this pace, though...

00:13:56.740 --> 00:13:58.220
Are you a demon?!

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:01.520
Just so you know, that chocolate 
you're eating is mine!

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.690
You got it from a kid at 
the dojo, didn't you?

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.080
Something wrong with that?!

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.250
Nope. It's delicious.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:13.080
Okay, now that we've replenished our nutrients,
 it's time for round two.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:19.400
That's enough already.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:23.600
It's not like I'll ever use math if I don't 
want to be a doctor or something.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.870
You might have to.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:29.880
Aren't there more important 
things I'll need?

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:35.690
Important things? You mean like 
using Hime's legs as a pillow?

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.680
Don't sulk!

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:43.420
Listen. People say it's useless if 
all you're good at is studying,

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.130
but being able to study at a 
school level is expected.

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:49.170
It just means you need to be able 
to go a step further, too.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:52.320
Or so my father said.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.150
That's pretty tough...

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:57.750
Well, in all honesty,
 I don't get it, either.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.950
But being able to do it beats 
not being able to, right?

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.050
My dad said

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.970
all you need is good looks 
and a smooth tongue.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.290
Wait, doesn't your dad practice karate?

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:10.050
So you'd better study, then.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:11.730
Your tongue's as sharp as they come.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.300
She's sulking again.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:18.750
There's no helping this girl...

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.130
You know, Nozomi-chan...

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:30.500
Aren't you worried that you 
might flunk out at this rate?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:33.810
If that happens, 
we'll be in different grades.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:37.580
<b>Class 2-1 
Kimihara Himeno    Kyoko</b>

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:37.580
<b>Class 1-1 
Gokuraku Nozomi</b>

00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:37.400
I'd hate it if we couldn't 
hang out with you anymore.

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:41.080
I want to go on field trips 
and stuff with you.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:45.170
They'd be lonely without you around.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:49.220
I guess I have no choice, then. I'll do it!

00:15:49.520 --> 00:15:51.220
This is for your sake, you know.

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.580
Hang in there, Nozomi-chan!

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.910
Snap to it!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:19.920
L-Look!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.140
What?

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.210
Uh... There was a UFO...

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:28.410
Look, Nozomi...

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:29.620
It's true!

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.250
I'm sure it was something else you saw.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:35.020
No, seriously! It was in plain sight!

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:41.260
Kyo-chan, if UFOs really exist, 
what do you think they are?

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.610
People say they're alien ships,

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.620
survivors of the Third Reich,

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.960
or vehicles used by 
Antarctican snake people,

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:50.580
but I don't know...

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.760
If they're secret weapons,

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:56.400
their development would demand
vast facilities, personnel, and money,

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.930
so it couldn't be some 
refugee organization.

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:03.420
If it were aliens, surely they'd 
have made contact with us by now.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.920
Then what about the Antarcticans?

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:08.580
I'm not sure...

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.640
Nothing is known about the 
level of their technology,

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:14.000
so I think everyone has their 
illusions about them.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:18.330
I mean, they look like reptiles, 
but they live in Antarctica.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:21.430
I do believe they have technology that 
the rest of us don't know about.

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:26.130
Still, if they had the immense chemical 
technology needed to build UFOs,

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.060
they probably wouldn't be 
at odds with America.

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:30.590
Did you know this?

00:17:31.640 --> 00:17:33.470
When snake people go to other lands,

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:36.230
they travel in a craft chartered 
by the Aztec Nations.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:39.700
Wow... Don't they have 
airplanes or anything?

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:45.240
Oh! Didn't the Aztecs have 
some kind of snake deity?

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.740
Right, Quetzalcoatl.

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.040
They say he drove away invaders,

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.880
but apparently, he really only 
served as a symbol of unity.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.310
Probably didn't have 
super scientific power.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.880
Here, drink this.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.370
Let's take a breather and then 
get back to concentrating.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.260
You don't believe me either, do you?

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.900
Well, I didn't see it, so...

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.720
But aliens do exist!

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:21.220
That's not really the point, though...

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:25.360
Okay, next up is potential energy.

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.150
Sure, sure.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:40.090
What's wrong, Nozomi-chan? 
You keep looking at the sky.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:42.130
I dunno...

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.550
Looking for a UFO?

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.030
See any?

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.470
Nope.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.120
Sure is a nice day.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.390
Yeah.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.140
<i>Furukanata. Furukanata.</i>

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:54.470
Oh, we're here.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.170
Isn't anything exciting ever gonna happen?

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.830
Nozomi, stop looking up while you walk. 
It's dangerous.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.200
Really? Jeez, be more careful.

00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:14.590
You know, I think...

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.760
today just might turn out 
to be a little unusual.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.050
What makes you say that?

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:21.730
Keep your head still,

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:23.920
and check out who's walking 
around other than students.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.270
Notice the swelling on his chest?

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.320
He's a public safety official 
in street clothes.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.240
Huh? It is?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.500
Not so loud!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.330
Stop glancing around!

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:47.550
But why...

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.770
Is that minister in town again?

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:52.510
The alumnus from our school?

00:19:52.510 --> 00:19:55.270
Wasn't he just forced to resign 
because of a verbal slip?

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.540
Maybe it's radical terrorism!

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:02.050
<b>Hitachi 
Electric</b>

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.590
Security's awfully tight though,
 even for that.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:06.790
It couldn't be a UFO, surely...

00:20:14.280 --> 00:20:16.950
Oh, Shigetoki-niichan!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.920
Milady?

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.180
Hey, what's going on?

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:26.390
Come on, don't be stingy!

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.010
You'll find out soon.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.140
Did you see those people outside?

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:35.510
Yeah!

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:37.510
I wonder what they're here for...

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:40.510
Huh?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.670
A new desk...

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:45.310
Is a new student transferring in?

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:48.310
It might have something to do 
with the security out front.

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:50.640
You don't suppose it's royalty?

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.770
Maybe not...

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:56.140
Well, there's no question that 
some VIP kid is coming here...

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:59.920
But this is just an ordinary 
public high school.

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:02.320
Nothing ordinary about 
that security, though!

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.990
Then who do you think the new kid is?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.620
Foreign exchange student, maybe?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:07.370
I hope it's a girl!

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:09.000
Does it matter which it is?

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.540
I'll introduce our new student.

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:23.270
This is Quetzalcoatl Sassassul-san, 
from Antarctica.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:27.830
I've come here from Antarctica 
to study with all of you.

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:29.800
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:33.680
I know you all have questions, 
so we'll save them for later.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:38.500
Now, Quetzalcoatl-san, 
please have a seat at that desk.

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:39.180
Yes, ma'am.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.290
Kimihara-san, show her the ropes, okay?

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.960
<b>You Can Tell What Type a Person Is by 
Whether They Believe in UMAs and UFOs or Not.</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>Antarcticans Are Like Walking Rumors.</b>

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:35.970
<b>But In the End, The Antarcticans' 
History and Roots Are a Mystery, Too.</b>
